@title dispatch-jobs queue backed up
@subtitle Quickpost Couriers on-call runbook, owned by Dispatch Engineering
@author Dispatch Engineering, Owner

kpi Alert fires at | > 5000 | for 10 minutes | bad
kpi Normal depth | < 400 | re-enable the scheduler below this | good
kpi Max consumers | 40 | the database pool limit | neutral
kpi Escalate after | 20 min | depth still above 5000 | bad

## Symptoms

- The `QUEUE_DEPTH_HIGH` alert fires when depth stays above 5000 for 10 minutes. Normal is under 400.
- Drivers see new jobs arrive late in the app.

## Diagnose

- Check the queue depth and consumer count with `kubectl -n dispatch get hpa dispatch-consumer`.
- Look at the oldest message age on the queue dashboard.
- Check the database connection pool, which is capped at 200 connections.

## Fix steps

1. Scale the consumers.
-- Run `kubectl -n dispatch scale deploy dispatch-consumer --replicas=24`.
-- Wait 5 minutes and re-check.
-- If depth is still rising, scale to 40, which is the maximum the database pool supports.
2. Check for poison messages.
-- Look for any message retried more than 10 times.
-- Move it to `dispatch-dlq` with the `dlq-move` tool.
3. Pause the bulk import scheduler in the admin console, because bulk imports add up to 3000 jobs at a time.
4. When depth drops under 400, re-enable the scheduler gradually.

!!! Never purge dispatch-jobs. Every message is a real customer delivery.

## Escalation

If depth is still above 5000 after 20 minutes, page the Dispatch Engineering lead and open an incident in #incidents.
